From 24dd480b78853761377c238c40096198d9784a53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fleet <fleet@local>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 09:46:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(e2e): production never receives a synthetic hand; certify
 the settled-hand trigger natively

tests/e2e/production-daily-missions.spec.ts certified the settled-hand Daily
Missions trigger by inserting a synthetic hand_history row into production
(table_id NULL, winners [], pot 600, hand_number 1.7e9-1.8e9) and deleting it
in a finally block. Every Post-Deploy E2E run put a winnerless 600-chip hand
into the live hand ledger; every run cancelled or timed out before its finally
left it there. Four survived (2026-09-11, 09-19, 09-23, 09-24) and raised the
cash-pot conservation no_winner_recorded monitor twelve times (board #5070,
incident e2e-synthetic-hands).

- The production spec no longer writes hand_history. Its step inserts the
  exact daily_challenge_event_outbox row the settled-hand trigger writes
  (event_key certification:outbox:<uuid>, threshold_values
  {big_pots:[499,500],strong_hands:[6,7]}) and waits for the live pg_cron
  drainer to book it: the receipt lands in daily_challenge_progress_events and
  the outbox row is gone. The spec never books the event itself, so the
  handoff, the outbox and the drainer stay certified in production. The wait
  is 180 s, above the measured drain lag (p99 69 s, max 173 s).
- scripts/ci/test-daily-missions-hand-trigger-postgres.py certifies the
  trigger itself on a private native PostgreSQL, loading the newest migration
  that defines fn_enqueue_hand_daily_missions and its trigger.
- The service-role request layer (serviceRequest in
  tests/e2e/support/temporaryCustomizationAccount.ts) refuses, before sending,
  any write to a hand or ledger table and any hand, rake, settlement, payout,
  jackpot or seat RPC (tests/e2e/support/productionLedgerWritePolicy.mjs); the
  one named diamond journal exception passes only for its exact table, method
  and reference prefix.
- tests/operations/production-e2e-ledger-write-guard.test.mjs reads the same
  lists and refuses any tests/e2e write, hand/ledger RPC or literal ledger REST
  path (fails closed on an unreadable target), pins the run-time refusal, and
  runs on every PR. The native certification runs in accounting shard 4, and
  classify-ci-changes selects that job when only the native script changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
